ccasional stray idea from the Old world of Darkness and hammering it until it fits smoothly in the Chronicles (currently have an ongoing project to turn the Kindred of the East Dharmas into Asia-based Covenants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:18:58-08:00","id":1012648,"title":"","content":"Who is Martin, what is his new direction for WoD, what is White Wolf's attitude towards CofD, and are we forming a posse based off of the answers to the previous sections of this question?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:21:49-08:00","id":1012649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1012648#post1012648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is Martin, what is his new direction for WoD, what is White Wolf's attitude towards CofD, and are we forming a posse based off of the answers to the previous sections of this question?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, Do explain please. As much as you can considering I'm sure NDAs are involved in this for those who in the thread who work for one of these companies","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:46:17-08:00","id":1012666,"title":"","content":"Here here Reighnhell,<br /> <br /> My personal favorite borrowings are from Ascension's Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts and turning them into Awakened Nameless Orders or making them Assemblies for the Free Council. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As for the original post, I believe the Translation Guides are going to the the only source of official rules for crossover between CofD and OWoD. That being said, the sandbox nature of both game settings does lend itself well to Crossover and idea insertion should anyone want to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-05-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T10:52:38-08:00","id":1012671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1012648#post1012648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who is Martin, what is his new direction for WoD, what is White Wolf's attitude towards CofD, and are we forming a posse based off of the answers to the previous sections of this question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Martin Ericsson is the new Creative Head of White Wolf. His new direction seems to be looking back on the themes of 1st edition Vampire:The Masquerade and create a multi media experience with a major focus on LARPing, restablishing the old meta plot, and tackling modern social issues in the setting. White Wolf's attitude to CofD has been pretty dismissive, they're super nostalgic for the golden age of the 90s and seem to irrationally associate CofD with the decline of their hobby rather then the general decline of the RPG industry that happened in the 2000s. Some CofD and WOD fans alike see this as Martin and White Wolf looking backwards and not forwards with the direction they want to take things and ignoring everything they and Onyx Path did for the last 15 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:29:26-08:00","id":1012690,"title":"","content":"Is that stance mostly just affecting stuff like the x20 editions and whatnot, or is it getting into Chronicles as well? Basically is the dude just trying to turn back the clock on Masquerade, or is he taking Requiem along for the ride as well?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:41:38-08:00","id":1012697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1012690#post1012690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that stance mostly just affecting stuff like the x20 editions and whatnot, or is it getting into Chronicles as well? Basically is the dude just trying to turn back the clock on Masquerade, or is he taking Requiem along for the ride as well?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>As of now Onyx Path has total reign over CofD, finished books are submitted to White Wolf for their approval before being sent out but that's about all the input they're putting in right now. The 20th anniversary editions are all Onyx Path too, but future editions of those games starting with the 5th edition of Vampire: The Masquerade will be done by White Wolf.<br /> <br /> CofD and Requeim and all your other favorite games will continue.In fact a new supplement for Requiem, Secrets of the Covenants is due out soon. However CofD will likely only remain tabletop games and won't get any video game or television adaptations unlike WOD. This is because they want CofD to remain a neutral setting toolbox with no set canon and also because they don't want any future brand confusion if the new WOD franchise takes off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:53:16-08:00","id":1012703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1012690#post1012690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that stance mostly just affecting stuff like the x20 editions and whatnot, or is it getting into Chronicles as well? Basically is the dude just trying to turn back the clock on Masquerade, or is he taking Requiem along for the ride as well?<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>They're pretty much just trying to sweep Chronicles of Darkness under the rug. Basically, Paradox bought the name White Wolf and the White Wolf IPs from CCP with the intention of turning Classic World of Darkness into a massive multimedia brand. Kind of like the Marvel and D.C. Cinematic universes, their vision for what they call &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; includes WoD video games, WoD TV shows, WoD LARP, WoD tabletop, etc. all sharing a unified setting bible and metaplot. They don't seem to have any interest whatsoever in any of the other White Wolf IPs, and in particular seem to want to keep Chronicles of Darkness confined to as small a box as possible to avoid any potential brand confusion with their One World of Darkness (which is also why the name got changed from New World of Darkness to Chronicles of Darkness). They've made a point in interviews to make it clear that they could have killed Chronicles if they wanted to, but decided instead to just let Onyx Path continue doing what they've been doing with it. They've taken pot shots at CofD whenever it comes up. Supposedly Martin loves Promethean, but in general the whole team seems to harbor a lot of disdain for Chronicles. So, while I'm bummed that our new Paradox overlords have decreed that CofD isn't allowed to be called World of Darkness and must forever remain an obscure PoD only tabletop game to avoid stealing the thunder of their precious WoD, I can at least sleep soundly knowing that it means this new White Wolf will keep its hands safely off of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:39:12-08:00","id":1012756,"title":"","content":"Which is ironic because honestly I think Chronicles is <i>way </i>more suited to a big shared-universe approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:57:24-08:00","id":1012762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1012756#post1012756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is ironic because honestly I think Chronicles is <i>way </i>more suited to a big shared-universe approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, but WoD does have a bigger preexisting fan base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:58:32-08:00","id":1012763,"title":"","content":"Thanks, folks! Good answers. Not as bad as I was fearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:13:48-08:00","id":1012771,"title":"","content":"I'm personally not worried at all about the direction Martin and Paradox folks want for cWoD. I know personally Dhaunae and I'm sure VV will be a great work full of love by their developers.<br /> <br /> And about CoD, I thinl the adquisition of WW by Paradox is the best thing for it. Currently OP is publishing more WoD than CoD books. We only have seen just one sourcebook for Forsaien and none for Requiem or CoD blue line (I know it's going to change soon). <br /> <br /> If Paradox is going to publish personally their WoD books, I hope this means OP gonna have more resources and time to publish more CoD books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:36:37-08:00","id":1012862,"title":"","content":"I'm far from sure about what to think of it.<br /> <br /> Certainly WoD is going to be treated with more than care, actual love. That doesn't mean it will come out well.<br /> <br /> Most of the worse bullshit in WoD during its life went from the game being made with love, not brains. For more than 20 years they managed to create ever better rules than the crap they use in WoD, but for the sake of love WoD retained the shittiest rules possible. The setting is great, huge, complex. But also full of inconsistencies, errors, silliness. With love they did CoG Tribe Revised, with love they did Gypsies, with love they made a rule for Abominations that serve no-one. With love they paved the road for Sam Height. I <u>fear</u> love.<br /> <br /> That said, maybe it goes well. It seems too focused on the past for me to bet on it, but maybe it goes well. Time will say.<br /> <br /> Agree with Charlaquin that it makes a good thing for them not going near CoD this way. It is a shame that they simply choose to ignore solemnly CoD, and this can come to hurt the game in the future, but maybe that's for the better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T17:06:16-08:00","id":1012876,"title":"","content":"Mmmm, indeed, passionate new creative leads can be a double-edged sword, and time will tell if WoD ends up cutting itself on it. To be honest, the new White Wolf has gotten me more interested in WoD than I've ever been, simply because I'm curious to see what they'll do. Those of us who aren't invested in classic World of Darkness will be able to pull up a chair and a bowl of popcorn and watch the situation unfold. Maybe steal some of the stray good ideas for our own games.<br /> <br /> Also, if they do succeed in getting a Netflix series, I bet I'll be able to get my parents to watch it, and that will be hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T08:31:40-08:00","id":1013182,"title":"","content":"It kinda bums me out, but from a business perspective, I do understand why they chose OWoD over ChroD for all the transmedia marketing, and I think it's a pretty valid decision. And I don't mind WoD, they're a fairly good set of games (albeit rather dated, being very much a product of their time, like any game).<br /> <br /> But it does really ruffle me how dismissive and unpleasant WW's attitude to ChroD is. It actually makes me want to avoid the original WoD. Like, you can enjoy two competing things, and it's weird how hard it can be for people to grasp that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:11:33-08:00","id":1013310,"title":"","content":"That's precisely the concern. It isn't a problem that they choose to focus again on cWoD. The change of name to Chronicles of Darkness was also an improvement, by itself. I dare to say that, until now, everything is going just fine and well.<br /> <br /> What sounds bad is their general attitude. Maybe they don't like CoD, but as the owners of the rights they should have some more respect for the people who likes and buys CoD. We are their customers, we pay for it.<br /> <br /> Also the love thing. Their declarations on WoD got me curious, but didn't made me confident. There are some potentially good ideas, but ideological blindness can hurt the game more than improve it.<br /> <br /> In particular, it reminds me of the same developers that created some of the worse traits of WoD IMO. The books that countered bugs in the rules saying that the ST should be an asshole, that there is no right way to play the game, except that there is, and you should harass as much as possible players who &quot;don't play right&quot;. That the fault is on the player for exploiting (maybe by accident) any hole in the rules or the setting. Specifically in the case of WoD, this attitude is what worries me more, and cWoD was full of this shit for most of the time, and it spread to some players as a disease. I saw good groups, good games, and sometimes good friendships being hurt by this view. Back in the days, a lot of people thought this game was sacred, and a lot of its books give credit to this view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:40:50-08:00","id":1013332,"title":"","content":"Once the next edition of WoD gets off will the Onyx Path staffers and freelancers be moving away from it or will White Wolf snatch them up? My reason for asking is that I'd like more ChroD stuff to be made and without the 20th Editions clogging up the works I'm hoping that comes true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:52:52-08:00","id":1013338,"title":"","content":"ChroD has plenty of people willing to bat for it, no fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T15:40:48-08:00","id":1013442,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, holy crap...that sums up 75% of my entire experience with CWoD. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Putting my two cents in here though, another pitfall that WW is missing is how dismissing CofD also means dismissing the experiences and polish that the OP has been putting into their latest project. More now than ever the Path has really perfected &quot;trimming the fat&quot; from their gamelines, and it especially show in the 2nd Edition core books. VtR 2nd Edition not only made me revisit the entire 1st Edition gameline and discover it's brilliance, but the 2nd Edition core book still remains in my opinion the most engaging book to read that the Path has yet to put out. That level of polish didn't happen in a vacuum, and by dismissing those pivotal experiences WW risks putting out products that are as dated to read as they are mechanically and conceptually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T10:05:08-08:00","id":1013815,"title":"","content":"That's the worry. It seems that they will keep the WoD lines to themselves, take it from OP completely (after the x20 line is out), dismiss CoD completely and focus on going back to the old stuff. With everything that went wrong still on place.<br /> <br /> What makes room for some improvement is their interest on forwarding the metaplot beyond the Time of Judgement. It literally means that they will take the setting at a point that makes it impossible to pretend things are the same. What that will mean for the development? That's a mystery, and the point of hope in this for whom cares about WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T21:06:42-08:00","id":1014135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1013815#post1013815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the worry. It seems that they will keep the WoD lines to themselves, take it from OP completely (after the x20 line is out), dismiss CoD completely and focus on going back to the old stuff. With everything that went wrong still on place.<br /> <br /> What makes room for some improvement is their interest on forwarding the metaplot beyond the Time of Judgement. It literally means that they will take the setting at a point that makes it impossible to pretend things are the same. What that will mean for the development? That's a mystery, and the point of hope in this for whom cares about WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, thanks to how all that stuff played out, the only ways WoD can go are way way up, or way way down if it continued from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T23:54:54-08:00","id":1014193,"title":"","content":"Theoretically, and there is my hope.<br /> <br /> But never dismiss the ability of humanity to surprise you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T14:30:26-08:00","id":1014455,"title":"","content":"I would personally be very interested in seeing sales numbers for V2ed vs V20. Presumably their 5ed sales will get similar sales figures at the very least. People keep saying that cWoD has such a larger player base but I've never actually met people in my area who play (or want to play) it anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T14:57:26-08:00","id":1014461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1013182#post1013182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda bums me out, but from a business perspective, I do understand why they chose OWoD over ChroD for all the transmedia marketing, and I think it's a pretty valid decision. And I don't mind WoD, they're a fairly good set of games (albeit rather dated, being very much a product of their time, like any game).<br /> <br /> But it does really ruffle me how dismissive and unpleasant WW's attitude to ChroD is. It actually makes me want to avoid the original WoD. Like, you can enjoy two competing things, and it's weird how hard it can be for people to grasp that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely. I was irked by the survey that WW sent out simply because they completely ignored CofD and I have zero interest in oWoD. I was going to say something about it in the comments section at the end... but no comments section. But, as long as they don't kill OPP's work, I can deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:45:07-08:00","id":1014892,"title":"","content":"As someone who didn't grow up with tabletop rpgs, my view may be skewed, however...<br /> <br /> I see WoD and CofD as two separate games. I have had one person describe WoD as 'Story with a game system tacked on' and CofD as 'A game system with a story tacked on'. I have a number of friends who hate MtAw because of the Atlantis backstory and the appearance of being more spellfocused (instead of just saying what you want to do with the dots you have). And I have a feeling that this is a true statement, more so when you look at CofD 2e.<br /> <br /> There have been a few sessions (in CofD 1e), where my group didn't roll a single dice. WoD I think could support this type of 'RP first, game second' style more than CofD 1e could. (I'm not sure how 2e handles, but given that bonus/penalties have been coded via conditions/tilts, I don't know if it would work out very well.).<br /> <br /> On the topic of conditions/tilts, it wasn't until these were created for 2e that I understood some people's hate for what was nWoD over oWoD. That oWoD was doing its thing to be a roleplaying system and that nWoD was moving more towards a rollplaying game (that D&amp;D seems to focus on in some groups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:17:20-08:00","id":1014912,"title":"","content":"The only place I can imagine seeing official crossover material would be in a potential Mage: the Ascension book that details &quot;Everett Volumes&quot; - parallel universes explored by the Void Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T13:53:24-08:00","id":1014943,"title":"","content":"The discussion of RolePlay vs Rollplay is a tiresome one, and I can't writ much today, so I'll try to be brief.<br /> <br /> Its bullshit. A ridiculous statement coming from people that try to hide the flaws of their work under the elitist premise that superior gamers should challenge their acting abilities, as if they were on the run for the Oscar, instead of in a room with half a dozen friends and snacks to tell a story no one else will ever know of.<br /> <br /> cWoD <u><b>NEVER</b></u> favored roleplay as a system. NO SYSTEM favors. That is what you need a system for, to take your place when you can't do that yourself. I played it without rolling a single die a lot of times. I also played CoD, M&amp;M, Shadowrun and D&amp;D (all editions so far) in the very same way. YOU don't need dice when you're in the mood for roleplaying and not rolling dice.<br /> <br /> What cWoD did most often was the contrary. By creating rules for social interactions, and bad ones at that, they made a lot of groups rely on dice when it wasn't needed. I have a friend who distanced himself from Vampire the Masquerade for years because of an ST who asked dice for EVERYTHING, and that was possible precisely because the system lends itself to such interpretation of the rules.<br /> <br /> nWoD was far more sounding as a system. And yes, this is good for people who wants to play dice. You know, people who only wants to roleplay shouldn't even care. 2nd Edition CoD went an interesting step for creating Conditions, and I actually liked it, you know why? Because it is a rule that ACTUALLY encourages drama. Because in WoD your only encouragement to accept some challenges is to be a &quot;cool kid who plays hardcore&quot;. &quot;The unbalance is to be realistic, if you're a 'real' player you'll embrace the hardships and take the weakest choice&quot;. This is freaking bullshit. A system that encourages drama is one that mechanically rewards drama. Yes, it is. Encouragement is recompense. You don't encourage a kid to swim saying that you'll break all the toys and shit in the water while the kid is swimming.<br /> <br /> Observe that I'm saying drama, not roleplay. Drama can be obtained either by roleplay or through the system, in a lot of ways. The Conditions system rewards drama by giving a Beat every time you resolve the Condition, that is, every time you make shit happen, instead of simply play along with current status quo. I fail completely to see where this goes against roleplaying. I said too much, and my hand is hurting, so that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T14:06:52-08:00","id":1014949,"title":"","content":"It's interesting how the edition war has turned into a cold one, full of passive aggressiveness. Disappointing, but interesting.<br /> <br /> A Crossover book would be a certain way to turn it into the old straightforward, 'Your game sucks because it's not my game.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2016, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T14:32:06-08:00","id":1014958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who didn't grow up with tabletop rpgs, my view may be skewed, however...<br /> <br /> I see WoD and CofD as two separate games.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. Like, explicitly and intentionally so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have had one person describe WoD as 'Story with a game system tacked on' and CofD as 'A game system with a story tacked on'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that argument before as well, and frankly, it's rubbish.<br /> <br /> It's pretty revisionist to describe cWoD as story with a game tacked on, because although it does have an extensive, convoluted story, none of it existed in the first edition. World of Darkness was a game first, and that game accumulated an extensive story by way of a continually advancing metaplot over the course of about ten years. Apparently, in the more than 10 years since that metaplot ended, people have forgotten that the 10 years worth of story didn't always exist. There is some truth to the fact that the rules system is clunky, but it only looks that way now because it has hardly changed at all since the 90's. Compare it to its contemporary systems line D&amp;D 3.5 and GURPS, and I would argue it's quite mechanically streamlined for its time.<br /> <br /> As for nWoD/CofD being &quot;a game system with a story tacked on&quot;, that's an attitude that comes from comparing nWoD when it was first released to CofD after its metaplot was finished. It's the same sort of revisionist view that fails to acknowledge that &quot;old&quot; WoD was new once too, but insists on assessing &quot;new&quot; <br /> WoD based on its entire history instead of its current iteration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a number of friends who hate MtAw because of the Atlantis backstory and the appearance of being more spellfocused (instead of just saying what you want to do with the dots you have). And I have a feeling that this is a true statement, more so when you look at CofD 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they don't like Awakening's backstory, that's cool. It's not for everyone. I do think the importance of Atlantis is far less than its detractors tend to assume, but to each their own. As for the focus on spells vs. creative casting, I disagree. Awakening's creative casting system is plenty robust, you could quite easily play a game of Awakening without ever using a single pre-written spell if you were of a mind to. What it does differently than Ascension in that regard is that it doesn't treat creative casting as inherently superior to pre-written spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been a few sessions (in CofD 1e), where my group didn't roll a single dice. WoD I think could support this type of 'RP first, game second' style more than CofD 1e could. (I'm not sure how 2e handles, but given that bonus/penalties have been coded via conditions/tilts, I don't know if it would work out very well.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, jeez. Look, I don't know why people think &quot;no one touched the dice all session!&quot; is something to brag about. This is coming from someone who's GMing style is specifically tailored to cut out unnecessary dice rolls whenever possible: just because you're not rolling dice doesn't mean you're roleplaying more or better, and just because you're rolling dice doesn't mean you're not roleplaying. I mean, the whole dichotomy is nonsense. If you're imagining yourself as a character in a situation and making decisions for that character based on that situation, you are roleplaying. Dice are just a random number generator to resolve actions with uncertain outcomes. There is nothing about them that prevents roleplaying. They can get in the way of narrative flow, which is why minimizing dice rolls can improve games, but that is a complete different issue than roleplaying. And if you're not using dice *some of the time* in your roleplaying games, what the hell are you shelling out 60 bucks a book for?<br /> <br /> Anyway, with that little rant out of my system, there is nothing on the system level that encourages or prevents you from playing like this. If you want to ignore dice, you'll ignore dice, no matter what the rulebook says. My policy of &quot;only roll dice to resolve actions that have a chance of success, a chance of failure, and a consequence for failure, otherwise just narrate results&quot; can be applied to absolutely any tabletop roleplaying l game system, period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of conditions/tilts, it wasn't until these were created for 2e that I understood some people's hate for what was nWoD over oWoD. That oWoD was doing its thing to be a roleplaying system and that nWoD was moving more towards a rollplaying game (that D&amp;D seems to focus on in some groups).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have more to say but my phone is about to die and I don't want to lose this post.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, got a charger. So, Conditions and Tilts are nothing new. Both WoD and CofD have floating modifiers and other effects. Take, for example, Presence/Majesty. Whether you're playing Masquerade or Requiem, you can use it to entrance a victim, causing them to feel trust and affection for you for a matter of days or weeks. The specific mechanical effects of such a trance and precisely how long it lasts varies from edition to edition and from game to game, but in all cases, you have to remember what the effects of Entrancement are, and those effects stick with the subject until the duration expires. Requiem 2e just puts those effects on a card and gives it a name. The most significant difference is that in Requiem 2e, these lingering effects are one of the primary ways of gaining experience. But it's a simple matter to change that if you don't like it. Just hand out Beats the same way you would exp (a Beat has mathematically the same purchasing power as a CofD 1e exp).<br /> <br /> The other big difference is that some (but not all) lingering effects in CofD 2 have opt-in aspects that reward you with a Beat (or a Willpower or something if you're awarding Beats the old fashioned way) for opting into them. Now, that's something that I can understand people not liking. It does require the player to make decisions for their characters that they might not make if they didn't have access to information the character doesn't have, which some folks find immersion-breaking. <br /> <br /> Take, for example, Spooked. Anyone with an ounce of genre savvy knows not to go off alone to investigate the strange noise, so players making decisions for their characters based solely on what would be best for the character (as a self-interested character probably &quot;would do&quot;) never leads to characters going off to investigate noises on their own. Unless the player just feels like doing something that's going to cause problems for the party for the lulz, which is generally bad RPG etiquette. And that makes it kind of hard to tell a horror story. So, CofD 2e gives you a Condition that encourages players with Beats (or Willpower or whatever) to decide their character gos off alone to investigate the strange noise, even though a self-interested character probably wouldn't, without being the troll player, by making it something that helps the party. Now, for some people, the fact that the system incentivizes players to make decisions for their characters that self-interested characters might not make kills their immersion. And while I don't agree with those people, I can empathize with them. But again, this isn't really a matter of system getting in the way of roleplaying. It's a matter of taste in roleplaying styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-09-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:03:38-08:00","id":1014966,"title":"","content":"CWoD combat had at least 4 dice rolls gor each action of each character each turn (initiative, attack, damage and soaking). If there were 4 characters and 4 antagonists that meant 32 dice rolling for just one turn.<br /> And that's supposing nobody had celerity or divided their attack dice pools... <br /> <br /> CoD resolves this with just one roll for character. <br /> <br /> So no, if there was a strong game in dice rolling was cWoD.<br /> <br /> And I loved cWoD and still love it, but its combat system just sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T15:45:34-08:00","id":1014976,"title":"","content":"I think the two games can coexist in the same multiverse. They are both valid and fascinating versions of the WoD, and they <br /> have a lot of similarities (especially among the Kindred) which could be attributed to the theory of parallel evolution. In my view, they <br /> are two separate timelines which diverged somewhere in the mists of prehistory, possibly with the Fall of Atlantis. HOWEVER, I do not believe in in-game crossovers between the two, for the reasons Charlaquin and Atamajakki already said, and because it cheapens what makes each game special by itself. Please let me know what you guys think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:25:18-08:00","id":1014992,"title":"","content":"Well, it's nowhere near &quot;official,&quot; but never say never!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/809400-umaraha-e-the-children-of-the-worm\">Umaraha'e: Children of the Worm</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/848028-mystery-cult-pentech-worldwide-leaders-in-natural-technology\">PenTECH: Worldwide Leaders in Natural Technology</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/777970-mystery-cult-initiation-walkers-of-the-silver-strands\">Mystery Cult: Walkers of the Silver Strands</a><br /> <br /> Plus a few other things scattered about, and more ideas in mind. I haven't had time to develop anything lately because I've been working on my own game, but I do have some plans for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T16:36:19-08:00","id":1014999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014958#post1014958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are. Like, explicitly and intentionally so.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've heard that argument before as well, and frankly, it's rubbish.<br /> <br /> It's pretty revisionist to describe cWoD as story with a game tacked on, because although it does have an extensive, convoluted story, none of it existed in the first edition. World of Darkness was a game first, and that game accumulated an extensive story by way of a continually advancing metaplot over the course of about ten years. Apparently, in the more than 10 years since that metaplot ended, people have forgotten that the 10 years worth of story didn't always exist. There is some truth to the fact that the rules system is clunky, but it only looks that way now because it has hardly changed at all since the 90's. Compare it to its contemporary systems line D&amp;D 3.5 and GURPS, and I would argue it's quite mechanically streamlined for its time.<br /> <br /> As for nWoD/CofD being &quot;a game system with a story tacked on&quot;, that's an attitude that comes from comparing nWoD when it was first released to CofD after its metaplot was finished. It's the same sort of revisionist view that fails to acknowledge that &quot;old&quot; WoD was new once too, but insists on assessing &quot;new&quot;<br /> WoD based on its entire history instead of its current iteration.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say WoD and CofD are two separate games I mean in the sense that before the name changed, in some ways nWoD was just seem as a new revision instead of a completely new thing if you didn't know anything else. That you would assume it was just like going from d&amp;d 3.5 to 4e. Given that my first game with the system was VtM (not sure which version) in 2009, my view is limited about the very early days and how it was.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they don't like Awakening's backstory, that's cool. It's not for everyone. I do think the importance of Atlantis is far less than its detractors tend to assume, but to each their own. As for the focus on spells vs. creative casting, I disagree. Awakening's creative casting system is plenty robust, you could quite easily play a game of Awakening without ever using a single pre-written spell if you were of a mind to. What it does differently than Ascension in that regard is that it doesn't treat creative casting as inherently superior to pre-written spells. </div> </div> </div>The arguments they gave me is that you can't even remove it easily from the Diamond Orders with how ingrained it is into their histories/writeups. As for the spells part, I suspect this is more of an writing appearance issue as the book makes it look like the pre-written things as the bulk of magical knowledge a mage can learn. That only the most powerful mages use Creative Thaumaturgy, as there is 100 some pages of spells, then some other magical things for another 50 pages and then comes the bit about CT at the end of the chapter (in 1e anyways).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, jeez. Look, I don't know why people think &quot;no one touched the dice all session!&quot; is something to brag about. This is coming from someone who's GMing style is specifically tailored to cut out unnecessary dice rolls whenever possible: just because you're not rolling dice doesn't mean you're roleplaying more or better, and just because you're rolling dice doesn't mean you're not roleplaying. I mean, the whole dichotomy is nonsense. If you're imagining yourself as a character in a situation and making decisions for that character based on that situation, you are roleplaying. Dice are just a random number generator to resolve actions with uncertain outcomes. There is nothing about them that prevents roleplaying. They can get in the way of narrative flow, which is why minimizing dice rolls can improve games, but that is a complete different issue than roleplaying. And if you're not using dice *some of the time* in your roleplaying games, what the hell are you shelling out 60 bucks a book for? </div> </div> </div>Perhaps an example: Say a character is chasing someone down some stairs. The Character wants to jump down the flight and possibly close the gap. Assuming the Character has the skill dots reasonably to do so, would you require a roll for this? Some ST would because by the rules it would. Some ST would say no, you don't have to roll because of the skill dots, and you just do it. Actions like this are probably minor compared to more social things. If someone can roleplay lying, in a believable way, would you still make them roll for it?<br /> <br /> While I agree that not really dice doesn't mean more/better roleplaying, I think in some ways it forces you to try to RP better because you don't have dice backing up your described actions.<br /> <br /> As for paying 60 bucks for a book for...it depends on the person. Personally I own 7 random MtAw 1e books that I have never used. I would probably even say barely even looked at. I really only got them because WhiteWolf had stopped publishing the books and I liked the game(I know you can get them all PoD now, but the non-full bleed pages, no page enders just is a bit of a turn off to me)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Conditions, tilts and beats] </div> </div> </div>I know it is more of just a matter personal dislike of how things are presented and it can easily be changed to be more like 1e as needed and any actual issues (like people taking conditions for the beat gain) is a matter of roleplay styles as you said.<br /> ------<br /> <br /> @Uxas said that oWoD combat was long and many dice rolls. I don't deny this. I think this is why I was always told that most groups avoided combat as much as they could because it was so long and drawn out. Or maybe it is part of the 'game system tacked on' bit. I don't know. My experience with oWoD games is very limited.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand as I didn't mean to have such a vague sounding post originally (sorry about that...), I don't think there is going to be an official crossover outside the translation guides. Anyone who wants to do a crossover can/will and those who want no one touching their preferred game line will be able to stay within it without fear of official designers trying to link things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12014-peraxis","name":"Peraxis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:33:38-08:00","id":1015025,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing about Atlantis in Mage 2E.<br /> <br /> <i>It never existed.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Atlantis&quot; wasn't even it's name back before it got erased from history. It was just some unknowable mage society that the diamond orders kind of try to emulate as best they can manage from what they can sort of piece together from a bunch of contradictory ruins scattered around the globe. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:09:15-08:00","id":1015047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say WoD and CofD are two separate games I mean in the sense that before the name changed, in some ways nWoD was just seem as a new revision instead of a completely new thing if you didn't know anything else. That you would assume it was just like going from d&amp;d 3.5 to 4e. Given that my first game with the system was VtM (not sure which version) in 2009, my view is limited about the very early days and how it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it was absolutely seen that way by many in the beginning. Heck, I came into Chronicles of Darkness in 2010, and I assumed it was like a 3.5 to 4e kind of thing. But that assumption was wrong. It was always intended to be a completely different intellectual property, with completely different game rules, in a completely different setting. This misconception was not helped by the fact that it was still called World of Darkness, which in retrospect was a bad decision, and while I object to the politics behind the name change to Chronicles of Darkness, I do think it is ultimately a good thing. To be fair, at the time the IP formerly known as New World of Darkness was meant as a spiritual successor to the IP formerly known as Classic World of Darkness, which was being discontinued, which I'm sure is a big part of why so many WoD fans have such contempt for CofD. But since that time, Chronicles of Darkness has evolved more into a parallel IP that exists alongside World of Darkness, which in retrospect would probably have been the better move to begin with. But, heindsight is 20/20. Anyway, point is, they are and always have been different games, and the perception of them being more akin to different editions of the same game is objectively incorrect, and your perception of them as two different games is objectively correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arguments they gave me is that you can't even remove it easily from the Diamond Orders with how ingrained it is into their histories/writeups.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not wrong. I just meant that the whole Atlantis thing is largely background and has little to no relevance to most Awakening characters in the modern day. To be fair, the 1e core book does an absolutely terrible job of conveying this, and in fact gives exactly the opposite impression. So much so, that I didn't have any interest in Mage until 2e came along and fixed everything. If they haven't read the 2e core book, I'd recommend them to check it out. The word Atlantis appears a grand total of 20 times in the entire book, three of which are in a quote from Neil Gaiman's <i>The Books of Magic</i>, and about half of the rest are in a 3-page appendix which is the only section of the book spent directly explaining the Atlantis backstory, and most of that is about explaining how Atlantis never actually existed and is more of a symbolic ideal that Mages aspire to.<br /> <br /> But, again, Awakening's backstory is totally not for everyone and if they still don't care for it, that's totally reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the spells part, I suspect this is more of an writing appearance issue as the book makes it look like the pre-written things as the bulk of magical knowledge a mage can learn. That only the most powerful mages use Creative Thaumaturgy, as there is 100 some pages of spells, then some other magical things for another 50 pages and then comes the bit about CT at the end of the chapter (in 1e anyways).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the nature of good creative casting rules is that they take up significantly less wordcount than a bunch of example spells. In 2e the general rules for spellcasting take up 17 pages, the last 3 of which are the specific rules for creative casting, and you could play the whole game with just that if you want to. That just speaks to the elegance and efficiency of the creative casting rules, in my opinion. That's a sign they're working like good improvised magic rules should, being simple and easy to use. Sure, the next 63 pages after that are taken up by pre-written spells, but that doesn't mean the game is more focused on the pre-written spells. That just means there are a lot of examples to choose from for folks who would prefer to push the &quot;cast Bigby's Icy Grasp&quot; button than make up their own spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps an example: Say a character is chasing someone down some stairs. The Character wants to jump down the flight and possibly close the gap. Assuming the Character has the skill dots reasonably to do so, would you require a roll for this? Some ST would because by the rules it would. Some ST would say no, you don't have to roll because of the skill dots, and you just do it. Actions like this are probably minor compared to more social things. If someone can roleplay lying, in a believable way, would you still make them roll for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, here's some GMing 101. Any time a player declares an action, the GM should go through a mental checklist. It looks like this:<br /> <br /> 1. Is there a reasonable possibility that this action could succeed? If yes, go to 2. If no, it fails. Go to 5.<br /> 2. Is there a reasonable possibility that this action could fail? If yes, go to 3. If no, it succeeds. Go to 5.<br /> 3. Is there a consequence for this action failing? If yes, go to 4. If no, it succeeds. Go to 5.<br /> 4. Determine the appropriate dice to roll to determine whether the action succeeds or fails, and ask the player to roll those dice.<br /> 5. Narrate the results.<br /> <br /> So, in your chasing someone down the stairs scenario, I see a possibility of success (jumping down the stairs could get them closer to their target), I see a chance of failure (they could mess up the landing), and I see a consequence for failure (falling on their face). So, I would ask the player to roll some dice. If the system has rules for jumping, I'll use those to figure out what dice to roll, otherwise I'll improvise a roll to call for. In your lying to someone scenario, there's not enough information to answer clearly. How well the player acts out lying really doesn't have any impact on the outcome, what is more important to me is the disposition of the NPC, and what specifically the character is saying to lie to them. For example, if the NPC trusts the character implicitly (either because the character has built a strong relationship with the NPC, or because the NPC is just really gullible, or there is some power or ability influencing the NPC's judgment, or whatever), if the NPC has no reason to suspect the character of lying, or if the player words the lie in such a way that the NPC would have no reason not to believe them, then there is no reasonable chance of failure. The action succeeds, and I narrate the results, no dice needed. If the character is hooked up to an EKG or the NPC has some sort of lie-detecting ability active, there is no reasonable chance of success. The action fails, I narrate the results, no dice needed. In this situation, the consequences of failure are obvious - the NPC knows the PC is trying to lie to them - so we can move on to the final step. If we've gotten this far, I'm probably going to ask for a Manipulation + Subterfuge roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree that not really dice doesn't mean more/better roleplaying, I think in some ways it forces you to try to RP better because you don't have dice backing up your described actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree with the concept of &quot;better roleplaying.&quot; Roleplaying is simply imagining yourself as another person and/or in another scenario, and making decisions based on how you think you or that other person would behave in that scenario. If you're doing that, you're roleplaying, if you're not doing that, you're not roleplaying. There's really no room for doing it &quot;well&quot; or &quot;poorly.&quot; You can <i>act</i> well or poorly while roleplaying, but I don't think a player's acting skill or lack thereof should impact their character's chances of success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:16:45-08:00","id":1015240,"title":"","content":"Elfive: I don't like that. If I ever run a M:tAw chronicle, I am using Atlantis.<br /> <br /> That being said, the core book does not say that Atlantis never existed. It says it was erased from the time stream, which is not the same thing. It's kind of like an annulment in divorce law: officially, the marriage never existed, but in reality, it did exist. Even Dark Eras makes reference to the Time Before.<br /> <br /> Also, if there is no Atlantis, where did the Exarchs come from and how was the Abyss created? This is not a sarcastic question; if you have an alternate theory, I'd love to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T07:45:00-08:00","id":1015249,"title":"","content":"If it was an annulment, it was an annulment of the cosmic variety. <br /> <br /> When I say Atlantis never existed, I mean that from the perspective of the history of the CoD, there was never a time when Atlantis ever was. The Exarchs have always been the Exarchs, They just haven't <i>always</i> always been the Exarchs. They were human once, but the people they used to be were never born.<br /> <br /> The Abyss has always not-quite existed, but it hasn't <i>always</i> always not-quite existed. Except maybe it has, because it's the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T08:25:38-08:00","id":1015256,"title":"","content":"There's really no proof the Exarchs were ever human, or that there was ever a time that the Abyss didn't exist. There is evidence of an extinct magical culture that could not have existed in the current timeline. But any details about that culture or the erased timeline in which it existed is speculation <i>at best</i>. Most of it is pure fiction that Mages willingly engage in as a sort of shared Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:09:18-08:00","id":1015327,"title":"","content":"Aaaah, this is exactly why I love Mage: the Awakening. Somewhere in the one of the Chronicles two Mages are having that exact same discussion just as passionately. ^_^<br /> <br /> And in the spirit of bringing this full circle, this lack of in-setting secrets and esoterica is something that I really found lacking in Mage the Ascension. Don't get me wrong, it's still a fantastic game. But, it's lack of truth seeking always made Awakening more appealing to me. Plus this disruption in themes would also greatly hinder crossover potential, since each gameline's magic technically wouldn't be able to function in the other game world. (I.E. No Consensus in CofD, no Supernal in OWofD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:20:05-08:00","id":1015330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1015327#post1015327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Plus this disruption in themes would also greatly hinder crossover potential, since each gameline's magic technically wouldn't be able to function in the other game world. (I.E. No Consensus in CofD, no Supernal in OWofD)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the World of Darkness was the Time Before, and Ascension Mages were the Atlanteans. The Exarchs could be Ascended Mages who destroyed the old world and created a new one according to their Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-10-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:23:08-08:00","id":1015331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1015330#post1015330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the World of Darkness was the Time Before, and Ascension Mages were the Atlanteans. The Exarchs could be Ascended Mages who destroyed the old world and created a new one according to their Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>O . O (...shock...)<br /> <br /> .......well, crossover problem solved!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T15:35:31-08:00","id":1015384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014966#post1014966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CWoD combat had at least 4 dice rolls gor each action of each character each turn (initiative, attack, damage and soaking). If there were 4 characters and 4 antagonists that meant 32 dice rolling for just one turn.<br /> And that's supposing nobody had celerity or divided their attack dice pools...<br /> <br /> CoD resolves this with just one roll for character.<br /> <br /> So no, if there was a strong game in dice rolling was cWoD.<br /> <br /> And I loved cWoD and still love it, but its combat system just sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agreed.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014976#post1014976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the two games can coexist in the same multiverse. They are both valid and fascinating versions of the WoD, and they<br /> have a lot of similarities (especially among the Kindred) which could be attributed to the theory of parallel evolution. In my view, they<br /> are two separate timelines which diverged somewhere in the mists of prehistory, possibly with the Fall of Atlantis. HOWEVER, I do not believe in in-game crossovers between the two, for the reasons Charlaquin and Atamajakki already said, and because it cheapens what makes each game special by itself. Please let me know what you guys think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they diverged at the Fall of Atlantis, though I recommend to you the read of Mage's Time of Judgement book, Ascension, the chapter &quot;A Whimper, Not a Bang&quot;. Just do it. That said, yeah, pretty much what you said.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will give my answer as <b>bold</b> after each section:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014999#post1014999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say WoD and CofD are two separate games I mean in the sense that before the name changed, in some ways nWoD was just seem as a new revision instead of a completely new thing if you didn't know anything else. That you would assume it was just like going from d&amp;d 3.5 to 4e. Given that my first game with the system was VtM (not sure which version) in 2009, my view is limited about the very early days and how it was.<br /> <br /> <b>And the thing is that such view is wrong, plainly put. It was an error, maybe, to present the setting as nWoD, but it was meant as an entirely new game line from the start. What's as going from AD&amp;D to D&amp;D3.X to 4th Ed is the movement from 1st Ed WoD books to 2nd Ed to Revised to 20th Anniversary.</b><br /> <br /> The arguments they gave me is that you can't even remove it easily from the Diamond Orders with how ingrained it is into their histories/writeups. As for the spells part, I suspect this is more of an writing appearance issue as the book makes it look like the pre-written things as the bulk of magical knowledge a mage can learn. That only the most powerful mages use Creative Thaumaturgy, as there is 100 some pages of spells, then some other magical things for another 50 pages and then comes the bit about CT at the end of the chapter (in 1e anyways).<br /> <br /> <b>Yeah, maybe was that.</b><br /> <br /> Perhaps an example: Say a character is chasing someone down some stairs. The Character wants to jump down the flight and possibly close the gap. Assuming the Character has the skill dots reasonably to do so, would you require a roll for this? Some ST would because by the rules it would. Some ST would say no, you don't have to roll because of the skill dots, and you just do it. Actions like this are probably minor compared to more social things. If someone can roleplay lying, in a believable way, would you still make them roll for it?<br /> <br /> While I agree that not really dice doesn't mean more/better roleplaying, I think in some ways it forces you to try to RP better because you don't have dice backing up your described actions.<br /> <br /> As for paying 60 bucks for a book for...it depends on the person. Personally I own 7 random MtAw 1e books that I have never used. I would probably even say barely even looked at. I really only got them because WhiteWolf had stopped publishing the books and I liked the game(I know you can get them all PoD now, but the non-full bleed pages, no page enders just is a bit of a turn off to me)<br /> <br /> <b>Ok, first, your example doesn't exemplify any distinction between systems. It is still on the ST. Second, it isn't necessarily better. Dice aren't rolled because it is needed, they are rolled because it adds tension. Maybe rolling dice in such a scene will only make we loose time, but maybe it will add tension and drama because of the chance of failure, even it being low. The narrative and the group's mood is the only parameter to say if rolling dice is a good idea. Third, depending on the group I would certainly let roleplay take care of everything. And depending I would never let roleplay substitute rolling dice, because sometimes players who aren't good as actors or at social interactions want to play a PC who is. Unless you're using RPG as a tool at training actors, players shouldn't be ever punished for not having personally an ability the character have.<br /> <br /> Forth, being forced to RP to cover for system failures isn't a feature for the system, it is a bug. cWoD have rules for everything CoD have, anyway, they just aren't that good. If a good system is one that forces you to Roleplay because it lacks rules for social interactions, you should play AD&amp;D 1st edition, or D&amp;D Basic. By the way, more people roleplayed a lot in those systems than most hardcore WoD players would ever accept.</b><br /> <br /> I know it is more of just a matter personal dislike of how things are presented and it can easily be changed to be more like 1e as needed and any actual issues (like people taking conditions for the beat gain) is a matter of roleplay styles as you said.<br /> <b>I think you're minding it far more than you need, but suit yourself.</b><br /> ------<br /> <br /> @Uxas said that oWoD combat was long and many dice rolls. I don't deny this. I think this is why I was always told that most groups avoided combat as much as they could because it was so long and drawn out. Or maybe it is part of the 'game system tacked on' bit. I don't know. My experience with oWoD games is very limited.<br /> <b>It was just because it wasn't revised. Forget about this thing of 'x tacked on it', this take on system won't take you anywhere. Even because with 3 changes on edition the game had enough room to develop the system, they just didn't. I also doubt completely that it was intended for discouraging combat, more probably it simply sounded realistic for the developers at the time (it isn't). And if it was intended as such, it is a poorly choice. Encouraging lateral thinking by making default response be covered by bad rules, seriously? This is obnoxious.</b><br /> -----<br /> <br /> Back to the topic at hand as I didn't mean to have such a vague sounding post originally (sorry about that...), I don't think there is going to be an official crossover outside the translation guides. Anyone who wants to do a crossover can/will and those who want no one touching their preferred game line will be able to stay within it without fear of official designers trying to link things.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T21:56:19-08:00","id":1015541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1015330#post1015330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the World of Darkness was the Time Before, and Ascension Mages were the Atlanteans. The Exarchs could be Ascended Mages who destroyed the old world and created a new one according to their Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Old World chronicle I've been in for years is looking like it might go this route next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T08:31:41-08:00","id":1015683,"title":"","content":"I agree. You guys have convinced me. I deleted all references to Atlantis as a real place from my timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:06:35-08:00","id":1016081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see WoD and CofD as two separate games. I have had one person describe WoD as 'Story with a game system tacked on' and CofD as 'A game system with a story tacked on'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would describe them as different games with different ideas, though I prefer CofD personally.<br /> <br /> I mean, the only WoD games that I can still get myself to care about would be Wratih: The Oblivion, which I have only played once and Mage: The Ascension, in which I only care about the Technocracy to be honest.<br /> <br /> CofD's system is more elegant and basically superior in every way, instead of having to think about required successes, difficulty, penalties and bonuses whenever I want any kind of roll (and I have to make like 3-4 every combat turn...), I only need to ask myself &quot;what's the penalty?&quot;.<br /> <br /> CofD resembles the First Edition of the original WoD to an extreme degree, filled with mysteries and possibilities and new ideas that were slowly exhausted and eaten up by the metaplot as time went on.<br /> <br /> Whether that is a good thing or a bad thing is up to you to decide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a number of friends who hate MtAw because of the Atlantis backstory and the appearance of being more spellfocused (instead of just saying what you want to do with the dots you have). And I have a feeling that this is a true statement, more so when you look at CofD 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also wrong.<br /> <br /> I used to <i>love</i> Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Back when it was released, I could shittalk on Awakening all day for not doing X or having removed Y or whatever, and I would often do so.<br /> <br /> But then Secrets of the Ruined Temple came out and I got caught up in all the mysteries and weirdness of Awakening, I found that the gnostic themes resonated deeply with my own religion (considering that <i>I am Gnostic</i>, this should surprise no one), I liked playing a refugee, fearing for his life and wearing a fake name in a prison-world overseen by harsh gods who could barely care about what went on below. I loved the feeling of danger as I investigated the shadows of Awakening, as I questioned existence itself and asked whether any of this was even real, I loved the symbolism and occultism and esotericism everywhere.<br /> <br /> And most of all, I love the fact that casting a spell is actually possible without three hours of arguing followed by two hours of whiplashes for <i>daring to light a fire with magic</i>. Ascension had a system for casting spells, it had one in First Edition, in Second Edition, in Revised Edition and it still has one in M20, this system consists of throwing a bunch of successes into effects and it very quickly got immensely broken.<br /> <br /> In Revised, the most balanced of them all, I could have a constant effect that reduced all Difficulties to 3 and went on forever and ever and ever and I could just run it as &quot;well im lucky u see&quot;. Sure, the Storyteller could declare it as vulgar, but that'd be a storyteller decision, and one that is easily fixed by simply casting such a spell as conditional so it triggers in specific circumstances and I suddenly just get a stroke of luck when necessary.<br /> <br /> But that's all balanced and okay, because if I got more than ten Paradox, I might as well rip my character sheet in two due to the extreme harshness of Paradox and the fact that the game named Mage incentivizes you to use as little magic as possible.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Awakening had an <i>actual functioning system</i> that would let me cast spells and be an actual modern-day sorcerer. My first Awakening character could bend space and the minds of men, he could step through walls and move himself along the hidden lines of reality that no one else could see, and he was <i>awesome</i>. Our cabal was filled with symbolism and hidden ideologies and agendas and the political landscape was a breath of fresh air from the Ascension War. It was a labyrinth of smoke and mirrors where everyone could be an enemy and we could trust no one, where every Pentacle mage could be a Seer working for the Enemy in disguise, where even Sleepers could be puppets on the strings of unforgiving gods and their cruel servants.<br /> <br /> And in that moment, I fell in love.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been a few sessions (in CofD 1e), where my group didn't roll a single dice. WoD I think could support this type of 'RP first, game second' style more than CofD 1e could. (I'm not sure how 2e handles, but given that bonus/penalties have been coded via conditions/tilts, I don't know if it would work out very well.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be the first to tell you that Conditions are annoying to keep track of, but I mean come on they are literally the same as just going &quot;you're sick and must make a Stamina + Resolve roll every month, success abates the disease while failure causes it to worsen. Dramatic failure makes it terminal and exceptional success causes it to disappear.&quot; The difference is just that they have <i>names </i>now, and are baked into the core of the system instead of being stuff you make up halfway through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peraxis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1014892#post1014892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of conditions/tilts, it wasn't until these were created for 2e that I understood some people's hate for what was nWoD over oWoD. That oWoD was doing its thing to be a roleplaying system and that nWoD was moving more towards a rollplaying game (that D&amp;D seems to focus on in some groups).</div> </div> </div> </div>The most intense roleplaying session I've ever had was in a game of DnD 4e, which everyone calls &quot;a game designed as an MMO&quot; while some of my most boring game have been oWoD's shitty four-roll combat system.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying vs rollplaying is an inaccurate dichotomy and has always been so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":6042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","user":"ManusDomine","date":". 03-29-2020, 02:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T00:29:14-08:00","id":1016446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1011781-tale-of-two-worlds-of-darkness-or-basically-would-there-ever-be-any-offical-crossover-material-with-wod-and-cofd?p=1015330#post1015330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the World of Darkness was the Time Before, and Ascension Mages were the Atlanteans. The Exarchs could be Ascended Mages who destroyed the old world and created a new one according to their Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my headcanon for years - a bunch of Traditionalists and Technocrats who finally figured out that maybe they should cooperate afterall to stop the end of the world. The optimistic idealists among them became the Oracles, the pessimistic realists became the Exarchs, and a few Nephandi who managed to slip in set up their own kingdoms in the Lower Depths.<br /> <br /> The Abyss is what happens when all the &quot;But Wait Source A Says Statement B About Topic C, So Statement D Must Be Wrong&quot; between various supernatural occultists gains metaphysical weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}